{'symbol': 'LUV', 'date': '2019-10-25 16:30:00', 'title': "Southwest Exec Says A 'Super Majority' Of Its Customers Say They Won't Change Their Flying Behavior Once The Max Returns", 'text': "SOUTHWEST AIRLINES CEO SAYS TRAVEL DEMAND REMAINS STRONG, FUEL PRICES REMARKABLY LOW.SOUTHWEST CEO SAYS CAPACITY GROWTH WILL CONTINUE TO SUFFER FROM 737 MAX DELAYS IN 2020.SOUTHWEST SAYS WANTS TO RESTORE AS MUCH OF ITS NETWORK AS POSSIBLE ONCE 737 MAX IS BACK, BUT WILL NOT RESTORE EVERY FLIGHT.SOUTHWEST CFO SAYS BOEING HAS PROPOSED TO DELIVER 7 MAX IN Q4 WITH REMAINING 34 ON ORDER SHIFTING INTO 2020.SOUTHWEST CFO SAYS ON TRACK TO ACHIEVING Q4 UNIT REVENUE AND UNIT COST GOALS DESPITE 737 MAX GROUNDING.SOUTHWEST CEO SAYS ANY POTENTIAL FLEET DIVERSIFICATION IS 'COMPLEX'.SOUTHWEST CEO SAYS SEEING A RETURN IN DEMAND FOR SHORT-HAUL FLIGHTS BUT IS SHORT OF CAPACITY.SOUTHWEST CEO SAYS EXPECTS MORE VISIBILITY ON 737 MAX IN NEXT 30 DAYS, DOESN'T RULE OUT HAVING TO EXTEND FEB. 8 CANCELLATIONS.SOUTHWEST EXEC SAYS A 'SUPER MAJORITY' OF ITS CUSTOMERS SAY THEY WON'T CHANGE THEIR FLYING BEHAVIOR ONCE THE MAX RETURNS."}
