{'symbol': 'VFC', 'date': '2019-10-25 13:30:00', 'title': 'VF Corp CFO Says FX, Incremental Tariffs, Ongoing Hong Kong Disruption Negatively Impacted Fiscal 2020 Outlook By About $0.07', 'text': "VF CORP CEO SAYS SITUATION IN HONG KONG MODESTLY IMPACTED THEIR REGIONAL BUSINESS - CONF CALL.VF CORP CEO SAYS INCREASING GROWTH OUTLOOK FOR THE VANS BRAND & NOW EXPECT 13% TO 14% GROWTH FOR FULL YEAR - CONF CALL.VF CORP CEO SAYS IN EMEA, UNCERTAINTY RELATED TO BREXIT CONTINUES TO IMPACT CONSUMER CONFIDENCE RESULTING IN SLIGHT DECELERATION IN OUR U.K. MARKET.VF CORP CEO SAYS DEMAND IN AND SELL-THROUGH HAVE BEEN STRONGER-THAN-EXPECTED FOR FUTURELIGHT - CONF CALL.VF CORP CFO -FX, INCREMENTAL TARIFFS & ONGOING DISRUPTION IN HONG KONG NEGATIVELY IMPACTED FISCAL 2020 OUTLOOK BY ABOUT $0.07 RELATIVE TO JULY OUTLOOK.VF CORP CFO -UNFAVORABLE FOREIGN CURRENCY RATES HAVE NEGATIVELY IMPACTED FY REVENUE OUTLOOK BY ABOUT $60 MILLION RELATIVE TO JULY OUTLOOK.VF CORP CFO SAYS FY OUTLOOK FOR THE DICKIES BRAND REMAINS SOLID AT 5% TO 6% GROWTH, VERSUS PRIOR EXPECTATION OF 5% TO 7% GROWTH - CONF CALL.VF CORP CFO ON TARIFFS SAYS EXPECT U.S. SOURCING FROM CHINA TO BE MORE LIKE 4% NEXT YEAR - CONF CALL.VF CORP EXEC ON HONG KONG SITUATION SAYS MARKET IN HONG KONG IS SMALL IN RELATIVE TO CO'S CHINA BUSINESS - CONF CALL.VF CORP EXEC ON HONG KONG SITUATION SAYS RESULTS THAT CO SEES IN CHINA ARE LARGELY OFFSETTING WHAT CO SEES GOING ON IN HONG KONG - CONF CALL.VF CORP EXEC, ON M&A AGENDA, SAYS CAN DO A REALLY BIG DEAL - CONF CALL."}
{'symbol': 'VFC', 'date': '2019-10-25 09:30:00', 'title': 'Vf Q2 Earnings Per Share Estimate $1.31', 'text': 'VF REPORTS SECOND QUARTER FISCAL 2020 RESULTS; RAISES DIVIDEND AND REAFFIRMS FULL YEAR FISCAL 2020 OUTLOOK.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.61 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.31 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.32 TO $3.37 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS EXCLUDING ITEMS.SEES FY 2020 REVENUE $11.8 BILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.61.QTRLY REVENUE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS INCREASED 5 PERCENT (UP 7 PERCENT IN CONSTANT DOLLARS) TO $3.4 BILLION.QUARTERLY DIVIDEND INCREASED BY 12 PERCENT TO $0.48 PER SHARE.Q2 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.26 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.QTRLY ACTIVE SEGMENT REVENUE INCREASED 9 PERCENT INCLUDING A 14 PERCENT INCREASE IN VANS BRAND REVENUE.2020 ADJUSTED GROSS MARGIN IS STILL EXPECTED TO BE 54.1 PERCENT.FULL YEAR FISCAL 2020 REVENUE FOR ACTIVE IS NOW EXPECTED TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 8 PERCENT TO 9 PERCENT.SEES FY CAPITAL EXPENDITURES OF APPROXIMATELY $400 MILLION.2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE IS STILL EXPECTED TO BE $3.32 TO $3.37.Q2 REVENUE VIEW $3.42 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $3.39, REVENUE VIEW $11.87 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QUARTER-END INVENTORIES WERE UP 10 PERCENT COMPARED WITH SAME PERIOD LAST YEAR.DESPITE INCREASINGLY UNCERTAIN GEOPOLITICAL AND MACROECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT, CONFIDENT IN TRAJECTORY OF BUSINESS MOVING INTO H2.'}
