{'symbol': 'WST', 'date': '2019-10-25 08:30:00', 'title': 'West Reports Q3 Adjusted Earnings Per Share $0.79', 'text': "WEST ANNOUNCES THIRD-QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.79.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.75.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.71 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RAISES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW TO $3.10 TO $3.15.Q3 SALES $456.1 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $450.9 MILLION.SAYS RAISING ITS FULL-YEAR 2019 NET SALES GUIDANCE TO A NEW RANGE OF BETWEEN $1.815 BILLION AND $1.825 BILLION.SAYS FY 2019 ORGANIC SALES GROWTH IS EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY 8%.WEST PHARMACEUTICAL - ACQUISITION OF INCREMENTAL MINORITY STAKE IN DAIKYO SEIKO NOT EXPECTED TO HAVE MATERIAL IMPACT TO CO'S FY 2019 FINANCIAL OUTLOOK."}
{'symbol': 'WU', 'date': '2019-10-25 22:30:00', 'title': 'Western Union Launches WU.com in India', 'text': 'Western Union launched its digital platform - WU.com in India, in association with YES BANK, one of the leading banks in the country, enabling customers in India to send money globally - 24/7. With WU.com customers fund their transactions online through transfers from their national bank accounts and then have the ability to send money into bank accounts in many countries across major regions of the world, including North America, Europe, parts of Latin America, the Middle East and Asia Pacific. The announcement executes upon Western Union’s strategy to expand its services across emerging markets and open new growth areas as the company leverages its core cross-border assets – including global settlement capabilities, network, compliance and technology systems – to enable international cross-border payments in minutes.'}
{'symbol': 'WY', 'date': '2019-10-25 22:30:00', 'title': 'Weyerhaeuser Company Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Weyerhaeuser Company announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced operating income was USD 202 million compared to USD 337 million a year ago. Net income was USD 99 million compared to USD 255 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.13 compared to USD 0.34 a year ago. For the nine months, operating income was USD 562 million compared to USD 1,217 million a year ago. Net loss was USD 62 million compared to net income of USD 841 million a year ago. Basic loss per share was USD 0.08 compared to basic earnings per share of USD 1.11 a year ago.'}
{'symbol': 'XEL', 'date': '2019-10-25 08:30:00', 'title': 'Xcel Energy Third Quarter 2019 Earnings Report', 'text': 'XCEL ENERGY THIRD QUARTER 2019 EARNINGS REPORT.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.01 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.03 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.60 TO $2.65.SEES FY 2020 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.73 TO $2.83 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.XCEL ENERGY INITIATES 2020 EPS GUIDANCE OF $2.73 TO $2.83..PLANNED CAPITAL INVESTMENTS OF $22 BILLION IN NEXT FIVE YEARS.QTRLY TOTAL OPERATING REVENUE $3,013 MILLION VERSUS $3,048 MILLION.NARROWS 2019 EPS GUIDANCE RANGE TO $2.60 TO $2.65 FROM $2.55 TO $2.65.'}
